{"author":{"id":"609bf866d4a5d716c19faf5d617b3bf3de478230d29602d72aad5aa90a80466f"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1791141302,"nonce":"Vky4kLjUvkUoCx5p6pm2wP4Ex0Y=","title":"install.sh can install a nightly, and every build reports version 0.1.0","message":"`ash --version` printed env!(\"CARGO_PKG_VERSION\"), and ash_cli's Cargo.toml\nstayed at 0.1.0 through v0.1.1, v0.1.2 and v0.1.3, so a release binary could not\nsay which release it was.\n\nSeparately, release.yml published the rolling `nightly` release with\nmake_latest: true, every morning (the scheduled run). install.sh downloads\nreleases/latest, so between the nightly run and the next tagged release it\ninstalled a build of main instead of the versioned release: e.g. the\n2026-10-04 07:44 nightly was latest until v0.1.3 published at 14:38, and the\nnext morning's nightly would have taken it back.","files":null}]}